# A note on glob semantics, because it is the easy mistake to make here:
# a pattern with no slash — `*.png`, `.dev-logs` — is matched against the
# path relative to the build-context root, so it excludes ONLY entries at
# the top level. Excluding the same thing anywhere in the tree needs the
# `**/` prefix (`**/*.log`). Both forms appear below and each one is
# deliberate; the comments say which is which.

# ── Source control ──
.git
.gitignore

# ── Build / dependencies ──
node_modules
.next
out
build

# ── Local secrets / env ──
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Local SQLite + covers (volume provides these at runtime) ──
data
**/data
**/*.db
**/*.db-journal
*.db
*.db-journal

# ══ PRIVACY — local-only content, mirrored from .gitignore ══════════════
# Everything in this block is kept out of version control because it holds
# personal content or machine-specific identifiers. The same reasoning
# applies to a build layer: the Dockerfile copies the whole context into the
# builder stage, nothing in the build or in the running image reads any of
# these, and a file copied into an image stays there for good. This block is
# separate from the build-noise block below on purpose — it exists for a
# different reason and must not be merged with it or pruned on
# build-performance grounds.

# The library itself. Mounted read-only at runtime; never baked in.
books
# Sample books used to exercise the scanner during development.
test-library
# privacy-guard: per-clone pattern file, trusted-network allowlist, and
# identity allowlist. All three name real local values.
.privacy-patterns
.lan-allow
.identity-allow
# privacy-guard: diagnostic log output, which may contain device identifiers.
# `.dev-logs/` is the current name; `.gsd-logs/` is the previous one, kept so
# an older checkout is covered too.
.dev-logs/
.gsd-logs/
graveyard-logs/
# Local assistant configuration, transcripts, and the agent mailbox.
.claude
.agent-comms/
# Autonomous-run scaffolding written on the machine that ran it.
OVERNIGHT_PLAN.md
NIGHT-LOG.md
ASSUMPTIONS.md
# Log and scratch output anywhere in the tree — recursive on purpose, since
# these are written next to whatever produced them.
**/*.log
**/*.hprof
**/*.tmp
# Key and certificate material, recursive. Nothing in the build reads any of
# these; the app's signing secret is generated onto the data volume at boot.
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/id_rsa*
# Files dropped at the repository root during review — screenshots, and stray
# books used for a one-off test. Root-level only, matching .gitignore: images
# that belong to the app live under public/ and must still ship.
Screenshot_*.png
Screenshot_*.jpg
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.pdf
*.epub
ink-prototype.html
# ══ end of privacy block ═══════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Editor / OS junk (build noise, not privacy) ──
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
.directory
.vscode
.idea
.codium

# ── Backups / scratch (build noise, not privacy) ──
.backups
backups
*.bak
**/*.bak
*.orig
*.rej

# ── Build cache (regenerated inside the builder stage) ──
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Test / docs (the builder never needs them; keeps the context lean) ──
tests
e2e
docs
.planning
deploy
launch.sh
playwright-report
test-results
